\section{Boxed vs. Unboxed Representations}\label{sec:boxed-unboxed}

The choice between boxed and unboxed representations is fundamental to the performance of a language implementation.

\subsection{Boxed Representation}\label{sec:boxed-rep}

In a \emph{boxed} representation, every value is a pointer to a heap-allocated object. This provides a uniform representation: all values are the same size (one pointer word) and can be stored in the same data structures.

