\section{Type-Safe Downcasting}\label{sec:downcasting}

Downcasting (converting a supertype to a subtype) requires a runtime type check to ensure safety.

\subsection{Dynamic Type Tests}\label{sec:dynamic-type-tests}

\begin{verbatim}
  let x : Animal = get_animal()
  let dog : Dog = x as Dog  -- runtime check: is x actually a Dog?
\end{verbatim}

The \texttt{as} operator performs a runtime type test and either succeeds (returning the downcasted value) or fails (raising an exception).

\subsection{Implementation of Type Tests}\label{sec:type-test-impl}

Type tests can be implemented using:
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Type tags.} Each object carries a tag identifying its type. The test compares tags.
  \item \textbf{Class hierarchy tables.} Each class has a table of its ancestors. The test searches the table.
  \item \textbf{Cohen's display.} Each class has a fixed-size array of ancestor pointers at known offsets. The test is a single array lookup.
  \item \textbf{Perfect hashing.} Types are assigned hash values such that subtype tests reduce to hash comparisons.
\end{itemize}

