\subsection{Layout Optimization}\label{sec:layout-optimization}

Modern compilers optimize the memory layout of objects for performance:

\begin{verbatim}
  // Source layout:
  struct Record {
    bool flag;      // 1 byte + 7 bytes padding
    int64 value;    // 8 bytes
    bool active;    // 1 byte + 3 bytes padding
    int32 count;    // 4 bytes
  };
  // Total: 24 bytes

  // Optimized layout (sort by alignment):
  struct Record {
    int64 value;    // 8 bytes (aligned to 8)
    int32 count;    // 4 bytes (aligned to 4)
    bool flag;      // 1 byte
    bool active;    // 1 byte
    // 2 bytes padding at end
  };
  // Total: 16 bytes (33% reduction)
\end{verbatim}

